AUDIO: 'Apple has decided to leave a 32-in gap [music] in its display lineup, and this might be the monitor that fills it affordably. Hi, it\'s Simon. This is the Miro Pro display. 32 in true 6K, full aluminum, glossy glass, one cable to'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your Mac. It\'s $1,300. Apple\'s standard studio display is 27 in, 5K, and 60 Hz for $1,600. The new studio display XDR version is XDR in 120 Hz and is still 27'

[00:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in, but it starts at 3,300. Neither of those are 32 in. And both of them are a little spenny. So, what do you actually lose by choosing something'

[00:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like this instead? Or are you just gaining in your pocket and on your desk? There\'s one spec that might put you off, admittedly, but we\'ll get to that because I don\'t think it\'s a deal breaker. Now listen, my search for the'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'perfect Mac monitor has been this elusive fight that I\'ve had for years. You find 120 Hz refresh rate, you lose any kind of nice design. You get 32 in and then you lose that refresh rate. You'

